# Architecture Rules

## Required workflow before implementation
- Read the relevant SRS section and `docs/OPEN-QUESTIONS.md` decisions.
- Inspect the existing repository and dependency contracts before changing architecture.
- Produce a short implementation plan with affected domains, data changes, APIs/events, failure modes, tests and migration strategy.
- Prefer the smallest architecture that satisfies the requirement and preserves future extraction boundaries.

## Layering
Use clear boundaries:
- Domain: entities, value objects, policies, invariants, state transitions, domain events.
- Application: use cases/orchestration, transactions, authorization policy coordination, ports/interfaces.
- Infrastructure: Django ORM repositories, provider SDKs, queues, storage, email, HTTP clients, observability.
- API: serializers/schemas, authentication, request validation, response mapping; no business rules hidden in views.
- Frontend: React presentation/state/query layer; no financial or authorization decisions trusted from client state.
- Realtime: Pipecat/Asterisk/SIP Edge adapters and session orchestration; core business truth remains Django.

Do not create a distributed microservice merely for folder aesthetics. Extract a service only with an explicit reliability, scaling, security, deployment or ownership boundary.

## Dependency direction
Outer layers depend on inner abstractions. Domain must not import Django ORM, provider SDKs, HTTP clients, React, FastAPI or infrastructure implementations.

## Data ownership
Every model/entity must declare its owner/scope and authorization path. Financial and audit history is append-oriented. Mutable projections must never become the source of truth.

## External provider abstraction
Define ports/interfaces around payment, telephony, AI/STT/TTS, storage, email, CRM/accounting and automation providers. Keep provider-specific mapping inside adapters.

## Async boundaries
Use background jobs for slow/non-interactive work such as knowledge ingestion, webhook delivery, notifications, reconciliation and scheduled hold release. Jobs must be idempotent and observable.

## Realtime boundary
Do not put slow billing, reporting or administrative workflows inside the realtime voice path. Realtime code should use short, bounded calls and safe fallback behavior.

## API contracts
Version external APIs where compatibility matters. Use stable error codes, pagination, correlation IDs and idempotency for irreversible operations. Never expose internal model structure accidentally.
